   "source": [
    "# 04 · Análisis No Supervisado — Clustering de Perfiles Clínicos\n",
    "**Proyecto:** Predicción de Hospitalización por Dengue — Bucaramanga  \n",
    "**Fase:** Segmentación no supervisada  \n",
    "**Origen:** `DengueConSignosSegmentado.ipynb`\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Propósito\n",
    "\n",
    "El análisis de clustering tiene un doble rol en este trabajo:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Rol exploratorio:** ¿Existen perfiles clínicos naturales entre los pacientes\n",
    "   con dengue? ¿Los clusters se corresponden con distintas tasas de hospitalización?\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Rol complementario al modelado supervisado:** Si los clusters identifican\n",
    "   subgrupos con distintos perfiles de riesgo, pueden usarse como variable\n",
    "   adicional en los modelos predictivos o para estratificar la evaluación.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Algoritmos utilizados\n",
    "- **KMeans:** Partición en k clusters esféricos. Eficiente, escalable, sensible\n",
    "  a la escala → se normaliza con StandardScaler.\n",
    "- **Clustering jerárquico aglomerativo:** No requiere especificar k a priori;\n",
    "  el dendrograma permite explorar la estructura a múltiples niveles de granularidad.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Consideración metodológica:** Los datos clínicos de dengue son mayoritariamente\n",
    "> binarios (1/2 → sí/no). Para variables binarias, la distancia de Jaccard o de\n",
    "> Hamming son más apropiadas que la euclidiana. Sin embargo, KMeans con variables\n",
    "> recodificadas a 0/1 y normalización es una aproximación práctica ampliamente usada\n",
    "> en la literatura de clustering clínico.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# IMPORTACIONES\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, \"../../src\")\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.gridspec as gridspec\n",
    "from mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import scipy.cluster.hierarchy as sch\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans, AgglomerativeClustering\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score, davies_bouldin_score\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "\n",
    "import config\n",
    "from config import (\n",
    "    DATA_INTERIM, CHECKPOINTS, OUT_FIGURES, OUT_TABLES,\n",
    "    COLORS, RANDOM_STATE, TARGET_COL, SIGNOS_ALARMA, SINTOMAS_GENERALES\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\n",
    "    \"figure.dpi\": 150, \"savefig.dpi\": 300,\n",
    "    \"figure.facecolor\": \"white\", \"axes.facecolor\": \"white\",\n",
    "    \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n",
    "    \"axes.titlesize\": 13, \"axes.titleweight\": \"bold\",\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "df_con = joblib.load(DATA_INTERIM / \"datos_con_signos.pkl\")\n",
    "print(f\"✅ DCSA cargado: {df_con.shape[0]:,} registros\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Preparación de la matriz de features para clustering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# PREPARACIÓN PARA CLUSTERING\n",
    "# Se usan solo las variables clínicas (síntomas + signos de alarma)\n",
    "# para que los clusters reflejen perfiles sintomáticos, no demográficos.\n",
    "# Esto permite interpretar los clusters en términos clínicos.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "todas_clinicas = SINTOMAS_GENERALES + SIGNOS_ALARMA\n",
    "\n",
    "df_cluster = df_con[todas_clinicas + [TARGET_COL]].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Recodificar: 1=presente, 0=ausente\n",
    "for var in todas_clinicas:\n",
    "    df_cluster[var] = df_cluster[var].map({1: 1, 2: 0})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Imputar nulos con moda (más frecuente para variables binarias)\n",
    "imputer = SimpleImputer(strategy=\"most_frequent\")\n",
    "X_clinico = imputer.fit_transform(df_cluster[todas_clinicas])\n",
    "X_clinico_df = pd.DataFrame(X_clinico, columns=todas_clinicas)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Escalar para KMeans\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_clinico)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Matriz para clustering: {X_scaled.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Nulos post-imputación: {pd.DataFrame(X_scaled).isna().sum().sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Método del codo y silueta para selección de k"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# SELECCIÓN DEL NÚMERO ÓPTIMO DE CLUSTERS\n",
    "# Se usan tres criterios complementarios:\n",
    "# 1. Inercia (método del codo): buscar el \"codo\" donde la reducción se estabiliza\n",
    "# 2. Silhouette score: mide qué tan bien separados están los clusters (max=1)\n",
    "# 3. Davies-Bouldin index: relación compacidad/separación (min=0 es mejor)\n",
    "#\n",
    "# En datos de salud, la interpretabilidad clínica del cluster debe validar\n",
    "# la elección estadística. Un k=4 estadísticamente óptimo pero con clusters\n",
    "# clínicamente indistinguibles no aporta valor.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "inercias = []\n",
    "silhouettes = []\n",
    "davies_bouldin = []\n",
    "k_rango = range(2, 11)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Evaluando número de clusters k=2 a 10...\")\n",
    "for k in k_rango:\n",
    "    km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_init=10, max_iter=300)\n",
    "    etiquetas = km.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "    inercias.append(km.inertia_)\n",
    "    silhouettes.append(silhouette_score(X_scaled, etiquetas, sample_size=5000,\n",
    "                                        random_state=RANDOM_STATE))\n",
    "    davies_bouldin.append(davies_bouldin_score(X_scaled, etiquetas))\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"  k={k}: Silhouette={silhouettes[-1]:.3f} | DB={davies_bouldin[-1]:.3f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Figura: criterios de selección de k ──────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Panel A: Inercia (codo)\n",
    "axes[0].plot(list(k_rango), inercias, marker=\"o\", color=COLORS[\"primary\"], linewidth=2)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"A. Método del codo (Inercia)\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Número de clusters (k)\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Inercia\")\n",
    "axes[0].grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Panel B: Silhouette\n",
    "axes[1].plot(list(k_rango), silhouettes, marker=\"o\", color=COLORS[\"secondary\"], linewidth=2)\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"B. Silhouette score (mayor = mejor)\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Número de clusters (k)\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Silhouette score\")\n",
    "axes[1].grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Marcar el mejor k\n",
    "mejor_k_sil = list(k_rango)[np.argmax(silhouettes)]\n",
    "axes[1].axvline(mejor_k_sil, color=COLORS[\"accent\"], linestyle=\"--\",\n",
    "                label=f\"Mejor k={mejor_k_sil}\")\n",
    "axes[1].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Panel C: Davies-Bouldin\n",
    "axes[2].plot(list(k_rango), davies_bouldin, marker=\"o\", color=COLORS[\"accent\"], linewidth=2)\n",
    "axes[2].set_title(\"C. Davies-Bouldin index (menor = mejor)\")\n",
    "axes[2].set_xlabel(\"Número de clusters (k)\")\n",
    "axes[2].set_ylabel(\"DB index\")\n",
    "axes[2].grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "mejor_k_db = list(k_rango)[np.argmin(davies_bouldin)]\n",
    "axes[2].axvline(mejor_k_db, color=COLORS[\"secondary\"], linestyle=\"--\",\n",
    "                label=f\"Mejor k={mejor_k_db}\")\n",
    "axes[2].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"Selección del número óptimo de clusters — DCSA\",\n",
    "             fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(OUT_FIGURES / \"12_seleccion_k_clustering.png\",\n",
    "            dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\", facecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print(f\"\\nMejor k por silhouette: {mejor_k_sil}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mejor k por Davies-Bouldin: {mejor_k_db}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. KMeans con k óptimo"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# KMEANS CON K SELECCIONADO\n",
    "# Se entrena el modelo final con el k determinado por los criterios anteriores\n",
    "# y la interpretación clínica. Se usa n_init=20 para mayor estabilidad.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "K_OPTIMO = mejor_k_sil  # Ajustar si la interpretación clínica sugiere otro valor\n",
    "\n",
    "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=K_OPTIMO, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_init=20, max_iter=500)\n",
    "etiquetas_km = kmeans.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_cluster[\"Cluster_KMeans\"] = etiquetas_km\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"KMeans con k={K_OPTIMO}:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Silhouette: {silhouette_score(X_scaled, etiquetas_km):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Inercia:    {kmeans.inertia_:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nDistribución de clusters:\")\n",
    "print(df_cluster[\"Cluster_KMeans\"].value_counts().sort_index())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# PERFIL CLÍNICO DE CADA CLUSTER\n",
    "# Se calcula la prevalencia de cada síntoma/signo por cluster.\n",
    "# Este es el paso de interpretación clínica: ¿qué define a cada cluster?\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "perfil_clusters = df_cluster.groupby(\"Cluster_KMeans\")[todas_clinicas].mean().round(3)\n",
    "perfil_clusters[\"N\"] = df_cluster.groupby(\"Cluster_KMeans\").size()\n",
    "perfil_clusters[\"Pct_hospitalizados\"] = (\n",
    "    df_cluster.groupby(\"Cluster_KMeans\")[TARGET_COL].mean().round(3)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "display(perfil_clusters)\n",
    "perfil_clusters.to_csv(OUT_TABLES / \"perfil_clusters_kmeans_DCSA.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Heatmap de perfil de clusters ────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(13, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "datos_heatmap = perfil_clusters[todas_clinicas].T\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.heatmap(\n",
    "    datos_heatmap,\n",
    "    annot=True, fmt=\".2f\",\n",
    "    cmap=\"YlOrRd\",\n",
    "    vmin=0, vmax=1,\n",
    "    linewidths=0.5, linecolor=\"white\",\n",
    "    annot_kws={\"size\": 9},\n",
    "    ax=ax\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Línea divisora entre síntomas generales y signos de alarma\n",
    "ax.axhline(len(SINTOMAS_GENERALES), color=\"black\", linewidth=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Etiquetas enriquecidas en columnas con N y %Hosp\n",
    "col_labels = [\n",
    "    f\"C{i}\\nN={perfil_clusters.loc[i,'N']:,}\\nHosp:{perfil_clusters.loc[i,'Pct_hospitalizados']:.0%}\"\n",
    "    for i in sorted(df_cluster[\"Cluster_KMeans\"].unique())\n",
    "]\n",
    "ax.set_xticklabels(col_labels, fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\n",
    "    f\"Perfil de síntomas por cluster (k={K_OPTIMO}) — KMeans\\n\"\n",
    "    \"Valores = prevalencia del síntoma en el cluster (0–1)\",\n",
    "    fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.savefig(OUT_FIGURES / \"13_heatmap_perfil_clusters_DCSA.png\",\n",
    "            dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\", facecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Visualización 2D con PCA"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# PCA PARA VISUALIZACIÓN\n",
    "# PCA reduce la dimensionalidad para graficar clusters en 2D/3D.\n",
    "# IMPORTANTE: PCA se usa aquí SOLO para visualización, no para clustering.\n",
    "# El clustering se realizó en el espacio original de 17 variables clínicas.\n",
    "# Proyectar clusters en PCA puede distorsionar la separación aparente.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "pca = PCA(n_components=3, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "X_pca = pca.fit_transform(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "var_exp = pca.explained_variance_ratio_\n",
    "print(f\"Varianza explicada:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  PC1: {var_exp[0]:.1%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  PC2: {var_exp[1]:.1%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  PC3: {var_exp[2]:.1%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total (PC1+PC2+PC3): {sum(var_exp[:3]):.1%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Figura 2D: PC1 vs PC2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "paleta_clusters = plt.cm.Set1(np.linspace(0, 0.8, K_OPTIMO))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Panel A: Coloreado por cluster\n",
    "ax = axes[0]\n",
    "for k in range(K_OPTIMO):\n",
    "    mask = etiquetas_km == k\n",
    "    ax.scatter(\n",
    "        X_pca[mask, 0], X_pca[mask, 1],\n",
    "        c=[paleta_clusters[k]], alpha=0.4, s=8,\n",
    "        label=f\"Cluster {k} (n={mask.sum():,})\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Centroides\n",
    "centroides_pca = pca.transform(kmeans.cluster_centers_)\n",
    "ax.scatter(centroides_pca[:, 0], centroides_pca[:, 1],\n",
    "           c=paleta_clusters, marker=\"★\", s=200, edgecolor=\"black\",\n",
    "           linewidth=1, zorder=5)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(f\"PC1 ({var_exp[0]:.1%} var. explicada)\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(f\"PC2 ({var_exp[1]:.1%} var. explicada)\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"A. Clusters en espacio PCA (PC1 vs PC2)\")\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=8, markerscale=3)\n",
    "ax.grid(alpha=0.2)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Panel B: Coloreado por hospitalización\n",
    "ax = axes[1]\n",
    "target_vals = df_cluster[TARGET_COL].values\n",
    "colors_hosp = [COLORS[\"secondary\"] if t == 1 else COLORS[\"primary\"] for t in target_vals]\n",
    "ax.scatter(X_pca[:, 0], X_pca[:, 1], c=colors_hosp, alpha=0.3, s=6)\n",
    "\n",
    "from matplotlib.patches import Patch\n",
    "leyenda_hosp = [\n",
    "    Patch(color=COLORS[\"secondary\"], label=\"Hospitalizado\"),\n",
    "    Patch(color=COLORS[\"primary\"], label=\"No hospitalizado\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "ax.legend(handles=leyenda_hosp, fontsize=9)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(f\"PC1 ({var_exp[0]:.1%} var. explicada)\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(f\"PC2 ({var_exp[1]:.1%} var. explicada)\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"B. Hospitalización en espacio PCA\")\n",
    "ax.grid(alpha=0.2)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"Visualización PCA de clusters — Dengue con signos de alarma\",\n",
    "             fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.savefig(OUT_FIGURES / \"14_pca_clusters_DCSA.png\",\n",
    "            dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\", facecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Dendrograma — Clustering Jerárquico"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# CLUSTERING JERÁRQUICO AGLOMERATIVO\n",
    "# Se usa linkage='ward' que minimiza la varianza intra-cluster (similar a KMeans\n",
    "# en esa propiedad, pero sin requerir especificar k a priori).\n",
    "# El dendrograma muestra la jerarquía completa de fusiones.\n",
    "# La línea horizontal permite elegir k visualmente.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Submuestra para el dendrograma (ward sobre N>10K es lento)\n",
    "np.random.seed(RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "idx_muestra = np.random.choice(len(X_scaled), size=min(2000, len(X_scaled)), replace=False)\n",
    "X_muestra   = X_scaled[idx_muestra]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 7))\n",
    "\n",
    "linked = sch.linkage(X_muestra, method=\"ward\")\n",
    "\n",
    "dend = sch.dendrogram(\n",
    "    linked,\n",
    "    ax=ax,\n",
    "    color_threshold=linked[-K_OPTIMO, 2] * 0.95,\n",
    "    no_labels=True,\n",
    "    above_threshold_color=COLORS[\"neutral\"],\n",
    "    leaf_rotation=90,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Línea de corte sugerida para k=K_OPTIMO\n",
    "umbral = linked[-(K_OPTIMO), 2]\n",
    "ax.axhline(umbral, color=COLORS[\"secondary\"], linestyle=\"--\", linewidth=2,\n",
    "           label=f\"Corte sugerido → k={K_OPTIMO} clusters\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\n",
    "    f\"Dendrograma — Clustering jerárquico (Ward linkage)\\n\"\n",
    "    f\"Muestra: {len(X_muestra):,} pacientes | Dengue con signos de alarma\",\n",
    "    fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Pacientes\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Distancia de fusión (Ward)\")\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=10)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(OUT_FIGURES / \"15_dendrograma_jerarquico_DCSA.png\",\n",
    "            dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\", facecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# CLUSTERING JERÁRQUICO — ETIQUETAS SOBRE TODOS LOS DATOS\n",
    "# AgglomerativeClustering no requiere submuestreo para asignar etiquetas.\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "agg_cluster = AgglomerativeClustering(n_clusters=K_OPTIMO, linkage=\"ward\")\n",
    "etiquetas_agg = agg_cluster.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "df_cluster[\"Cluster_Jerarquico\"] = etiquetas_agg\n",
    "\n",
    "sil_agg = silhouette_score(X_scaled, etiquetas_agg, sample_size=5000, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "print(f\"Silhouette clustering jerárquico (k={K_OPTIMO}): {sil_agg:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Comparar tasas de hospitalización por cluster en ambos métodos\n",
    "hosp_km  = df_cluster.groupby(\"Cluster_KMeans\")[TARGET_COL].agg([\"mean\", \"size\"]).round(3)\n",
    "hosp_agg = df_cluster.groupby(\"Cluster_Jerarquico\")[TARGET_COL].agg([\"mean\", \"size\"]).round(3)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTasa hospitalización por cluster — KMeans:\")\n",
    "display(hosp_km.rename(columns={\"mean\": \"Pct_Hosp\", \"size\": \"N\"}))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTasa hospitalización por cluster — Jerárquico:\")\n",
    "display(hosp_agg.rename(columns={\"mean\": \"Pct_Hosp\", \"size\": \"N\"}))"
   ]
  },
